        "original_id": "6a0111a4-93fc-5772-8100-d618eea682e4",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Toshi, Toshimitsu Deyama, Warrel Dane\n- Bands: X Japan, Sanctuary\n- Places: Tateyama, Chiba, Tokyo Dome\n- Roles: singer, songwriter, lead vocalist, co-founder\n- Events: X Japan disbanding, Art of Life 1993.12.31 Tokyo Dome live concerts\n- Topics: studio software vocal touch-ups\n\nFacts:\n- Toshimitsu Deyama was born on October 10, 1965, in Tateyama, Chiba.\n- Toshimitsu Deyama is known exclusively by the stage name Toshi and is a Japanese singer and songwriter.\n- Some parts of Toshi's vocals on Art of Life 1993.12.31 Tokyo Dome were touched up by studio software to compensate for apparent faults at both live concerts.\n- X Japan disbanded in 1997.\n- Toshi was a co-founder of X Japan and is best known as its lead vocalist.\n- Warrel Dane was born on March 7, 1969.\n- Warrel Dane is the lead singer of the American power metal band Sanctuary.",
